slml 0.2
use"layout.slml"

@card{bg#fff p20 r12 b1 bc#e4e4ea g6}
@highlight{bg#fff4d6 bc#f0d48a}

doc{$title"Boxes and styles"
  t.lead"Every block element is a box. Its appearance is set with attributes, and sets of attributes you use often become *styles*."
  section{$id"box" $title"The box"
    c{g0
      ref{$name"padding" $values"number" $about"Space inside the box on all sides."}
      ref{$name"padding-x / -y" $values"number" $about"Horizontal or vertical padding only; they override padding."}
      ref{$name"fill" $values"color" $about"Background color."}
      ref{$name"radius" $values"number" $about"Rounded corners."}
      ref{$name"border" $values"number" $about"Border width. Its color is border-color (light gray by default)."}
      ref{$name"shadow" $values"none / small / large" $about"A soft drop shadow."}
    }
    demo{$code"column(fill: #ffffff, padding: 20, radius: 12,\n       border: 1, border-color: #e4e4ea, shadow: small) {\n  heading(level: 3) \"A card\"\n  text \"Padding, fill, radius, border and shadow.\"\n}"
      c{bg#fff p20 r12 b1 bc#e4e4ea sh:s
        ###"A card"
        "Padding, fill, radius, border and shadow."
      }
    }
    note{$title"Sizes include padding and border"
      "A box with `width: 200` and `padding: 20` is 200 pixels wide in total. There is no box-model arithmetic to remember."
    }
  }
  section{$id"styles" $title"Styles"
    "A `style` gives a name to a set of attributes. Apply it with a dot after the element name. The element's own attributes win over the style's:"
    demo{$code"style card(fill: #ffffff, padding: 20, radius: 12,\n           border: 1, border-color: #e4e4ea, gap: 6)\nstyle highlight(fill: #fff4d6, border-color: #f0d48a)\n\nrow(gap: 12) {\n  column.card(width: fill) { text \"Plain card\" }\n  column.card.highlight(width: fill) { text \"Card + highlight\" }\n  column.card(width: fill, radius: 0) { text \"Square card\" }\n}"
      r{g12
        c.card{w:f "Plain card"}
        c.card.highlight{w:f "Card + highlight"}
        c.card{w:f r0 "Square card"}
      }
    }
    -{g6
      "Styles are applied left to right, then the element's own attributes: `column.card.highlight(radius: 0)`."
      "A style may only contain attributes that fit every element it is used on; `text.card` is an error here, because a text has no `gap`."
      "Styles never cascade and have no selectors. An element looks the way its own line says."
      "Put styles you share between pages into a library file and `use` it. See [imports](/components.slml#imports)."
    }
  }
  section{$id"colors" $title"Colors"
    "Colors are hexadecimal: `#rgb`, `#rrggbb`, or with transparency `#rgba` / `#rrggbbaa`. There are no color names, so a color always means the same thing."
    r{g8 wrap
      t{bg#2457d6 c#fff p10 r8 "#2457d6"}
      t{bg#146c43 c#fff p10 r8 "#146c43"}
      t{bg#b42318 c#fff p10 r8 "#b42318"}
      t{bg#00000014 p10 r8 "#00000014"}
    }
  }
  pager{$prev"/layout-guide.slml" $prev-label"Layout" $next"/content.slml" $next-label"Lists, code and images"}
}
